Title: this is an example of time-series regression of y on x 
        with lag-1 autoregressive effects
MONTECARLO:  NAMES ARE y x;
             NOBS = 100;
             NREP = 1;
             LAGGED = y(1) x(1);
             SAVE = ex6.24.dat;
MODEL POPULATION:
            x*1;
            y ON x*.7;
            y ON y&1*.2 x&1*.4; 
            y*1;
            x ON x&1*.5;
ANALYSIS: 
    		ESTIMATOR = BAYES;  
            BITERATIONS = (500); 
            PROCESSORS = 2;
MODEL:
            y ON x*.7;
            y ON y&1*.2 x&1*.4; 
            y*1;
            x ON x&1*.5;
OUTPUT:     TECH8;